WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.430
- Good morning Believe
Nation, today's message

00:00:02.430 --> 00:00:04.945
is make your presence count.

00:00:04.945 --> 00:00:06.902
Over to you Trey Songz.

00:00:06.902 --> 00:00:08.740
(rooster crowing)

00:00:08.740 --> 00:00:11.586
♫ I wake up every morning

00:00:11.586 --> 00:00:14.272
♫ Entpresso keep me going

00:00:14.272 --> 00:00:18.465
♫ I wake up every morning

00:00:18.465 --> 00:00:19.298
- There was a point
where I was putting out

00:00:19.298 --> 00:00:21.131
a new song every week.

00:00:22.686 --> 00:00:26.341
It was, Trey Songz music
Monday, I put out a new song

00:00:26.341 --> 00:00:29.502
every Monday for like
two and a half months.

00:00:29.502 --> 00:00:31.126
Before my mix tape came out,

00:00:31.126 --> 00:00:32.693
which was Anticipation, which got

00:00:32.693 --> 00:00:35.443
50,000 downloads the first night.

00:00:37.080 --> 00:00:38.593
Ready came out.

00:00:38.593 --> 00:00:40.599
Ready's had six or seven singles

00:00:40.599 --> 00:00:42.630
I think that has a lot to do with it.

00:00:42.630 --> 00:00:44.169
Going on tour with Jay-Z,

00:00:44.169 --> 00:00:45.762
who's an international superstar.

00:00:45.762 --> 00:00:50.053
That definitely brings a
lot of attention to my name.

00:00:50.053 --> 00:00:54.287
I performed with Stevie
Wonder on the BET Honors.

00:00:54.287 --> 00:00:56.684
I kissed Toni Braxton on stage.

00:00:56.684 --> 00:00:59.816
It was a lot of steps
toward where I am now

00:00:59.816 --> 00:01:02.947
and I think that it's
just beginning even still.

00:01:02.947 --> 00:01:07.856
That's why this run is so
jam packed, my schedule.

00:01:07.856 --> 00:01:09.610
That's why I'm in a
different country everyday

00:01:09.610 --> 00:01:11.250
cause I need to make my presence felt

00:01:11.250 --> 00:01:13.551
and even when I come back next time

00:01:13.551 --> 00:01:15.834
I'll work even harder
to make my presence felt

00:01:15.834 --> 00:01:19.831
because I'm working here
this time like I'm a new act.

00:01:19.831 --> 00:01:21.570
My manager told me we gon'
come out here and we gon

00:01:21.570 --> 00:01:25.031
act like it's 2005 and what that means is

00:01:25.031 --> 00:01:27.446
act like I just got to make it.

00:01:27.446 --> 00:01:31.613
So, I don't feel as though
I'm a superstar here yet.

00:01:33.439 --> 00:01:34.737
I'm working my way there.

00:01:34.737 --> 00:01:36.558
- So one of my personal goals is to

00:01:36.558 --> 00:01:39.203
wherever I go that my presence is felt.

00:01:39.203 --> 00:01:41.824
I want to make sure that the
thing I'm spending my time on

00:01:41.824 --> 00:01:42.753
has an impact.

00:01:42.753 --> 00:01:44.557
I'm heavily driven by impact.

00:01:44.557 --> 00:01:46.298
And it's not from an ego point of view,

00:01:46.298 --> 00:01:48.193
not that when I walk into a room

00:01:48.193 --> 00:01:49.461
you need to worship me,

00:01:49.461 --> 00:01:50.636
that's not the goal,

00:01:50.636 --> 00:01:52.472
but wherever I'm spending my time

00:01:52.472 --> 00:01:55.480
that things are going to get better.

00:01:55.480 --> 00:01:57.319
That if I'm spending my
time in this business

00:01:57.319 --> 00:01:58.532
this business is going to get better

00:01:58.532 --> 00:01:59.549
and it's going to help the community.

00:01:59.549 --> 00:02:01.921
If I'm spending time making videos for you

00:02:01.921 --> 00:02:03.867
that you are digesting them

00:02:03.867 --> 00:02:05.487
and using them and helping them

00:02:05.487 --> 00:02:07.794
to make you get better and
build awesome businesses

00:02:07.794 --> 00:02:09.577
that impact our culture.

00:02:09.577 --> 00:02:10.410
It's the goal.

00:02:10.410 --> 00:02:12.885
If I felt like these videos were not

00:02:12.885 --> 00:02:16.311
having an impact on you then
I would stop making them.

00:02:16.311 --> 00:02:18.028
I would still consume them for myself

00:02:18.028 --> 00:02:20.413
cause the number of
habits that I've picked up

00:02:20.413 --> 00:02:23.330
that it wasn't having
an impact on you guys

00:02:23.330 --> 00:02:26.083
but has an impact on me so I
just keep doing it for myself.

00:02:26.083 --> 00:02:28.349
I look at the morning
gratitude series as an example.

00:02:28.349 --> 00:02:30.194
I had a youtube series where everyday

00:02:30.194 --> 00:02:32.755
I went on and shared three
things I was grateful for

00:02:32.755 --> 00:02:34.948
and encouraged you guys to
come on and do it with me.

00:02:34.948 --> 00:02:37.205
And we had a good loyal
audience coming and doing it

00:02:37.205 --> 00:02:39.284
but it wasn't having an impact I wanted

00:02:39.284 --> 00:02:41.022
and so I cut the series.

00:02:41.022 --> 00:02:43.023
I still do it personally
every morning with my wife,

00:02:43.023 --> 00:02:45.909
but I don't share it with you guys

00:02:45.909 --> 00:02:47.744
because I want to make
sure that the things

00:02:47.744 --> 00:02:51.510
that I'm spending my
time on is worth while.

00:02:51.510 --> 00:02:53.252
I think everybody should have the opinion

00:02:53.252 --> 00:02:55.790
that wherever you walk into,
whatever room you're in,

00:02:55.790 --> 00:02:57.613
whatever business you're in,

00:02:57.613 --> 00:02:59.294
you're going to make it better.

00:02:59.294 --> 00:03:00.944
It's your goal to make it better.

00:03:00.944 --> 00:03:02.634
Again, not from and ego point of view,

00:03:02.634 --> 00:03:04.375
that I'm amazing and I'm going to do this,

00:03:04.375 --> 00:03:06.683
but from a genuine desire
to make things better,

00:03:06.683 --> 00:03:08.545
to help people, to elevate, to lift.

00:03:08.545 --> 00:03:10.813
If you are not making things better,

00:03:10.813 --> 00:03:12.268
you're either making things worse,

00:03:12.268 --> 00:03:13.101
which isn't great,

00:03:13.101 --> 00:03:14.082
or you're just apathetic

00:03:14.082 --> 00:03:15.876
and is that the life
that you want to live?

00:03:15.876 --> 00:03:18.521
Do you want to walk around
going into all these rooms

00:03:18.521 --> 00:03:21.029
and the rooms are your
life, your business,

00:03:21.029 --> 00:03:23.717
your friends, these different rooms

00:03:23.717 --> 00:03:25.593
of you daily existence and just be

00:03:25.593 --> 00:03:28.063
apathetic and not really
caring what happens?

00:03:28.063 --> 00:03:29.562
Where if you go in with the intention of

00:03:29.562 --> 00:03:33.463
my time matters, my life here is limited,

00:03:33.463 --> 00:03:35.687
I want to make every second count.

00:03:35.687 --> 00:03:38.230
It shifts your perspective

00:03:38.230 --> 00:03:39.779
and I think it's really important.

00:03:39.779 --> 00:03:41.329
One of the things I do on
a fairly consistent basis

00:03:41.329 --> 00:03:42.965
is look at my schedule.

00:03:42.965 --> 00:03:44.529
I look at where am I spending my time.

00:03:44.529 --> 00:03:46.446
I live and die by my calendar.

00:03:46.446 --> 00:03:48.105
Where am I spending my time

00:03:48.105 --> 00:03:50.090
is the most precious asset that I have,

00:03:50.090 --> 00:03:51.291
I'm never getting it back,

00:03:51.291 --> 00:03:52.551
Where am I spending it?

00:03:52.551 --> 00:03:54.228
And doing a constant audit of

00:03:54.228 --> 00:03:57.002
are these the right places?

00:03:57.002 --> 00:03:59.236
Should I still be making youtube videos?

00:03:59.236 --> 00:04:00.470
Should I invest that time to go off

00:04:00.470 --> 00:04:02.642
and do something else, or not?

00:04:02.642 --> 00:04:04.817
And the things that always
tips the balance for me

00:04:04.817 --> 00:04:08.851
is are these things leading
to a major impact or not?

00:04:08.851 --> 00:04:11.524
My goal is to help a
billion entrepreneurs.

00:04:11.524 --> 00:04:13.109
Whether I reach that goal
or not it doesn't matter.

00:04:13.109 --> 00:04:16.858
It's the process, it's
the work that I'm doing

00:04:16.858 --> 00:04:20.878
has to have the potential to
help a billion entrepreneurs.

00:04:20.878 --> 00:04:22.322
If it does, I'm into it.

00:04:22.322 --> 00:04:24.460
If it's not, I'm not going to do it.

00:04:24.460 --> 00:04:26.377
And I encourage you to value your time

00:04:26.377 --> 00:04:28.982
more preciously and to do a severe audit

00:04:28.982 --> 00:04:31.204
to look at where you're spending you time

00:04:31.204 --> 00:04:34.555
and are you having a positive
impact on your customers,

00:04:34.555 --> 00:04:37.484
on your suppliers, on your
friends, on your relationships,

00:04:37.484 --> 00:04:39.158
and everybody around you.

00:04:39.158 --> 00:04:40.533
Make your time count.

00:04:40.533 --> 00:04:42.276
So the question today is I'm curious

00:04:42.276 --> 00:04:45.799
what are you spending time on
that you probably shouldn't?

00:04:45.799 --> 00:04:47.367
That's not really having an impact,

00:04:47.367 --> 00:04:48.943
that you're not making your presence felt,

00:04:48.943 --> 00:04:50.296
where are you wasting your time

00:04:50.296 --> 00:04:52.288
that you want to change in
your life or your business?

00:04:52.288 --> 00:04:53.589
Leave it in the comments below

00:04:53.589 --> 00:04:54.873
I'm super curious to find out.

00:04:54.873 --> 00:04:56.678
I also want to give a quick
shout out to Ibby Hadeed

00:04:56.678 --> 00:04:58.743
thank you so much Ibby
for picking up a copy

00:04:58.743 --> 00:05:00.678
of my book "Your One
Word" it really really

00:05:00.678 --> 00:05:02.449
means a lot to me and I really hope

00:05:02.449 --> 00:05:04.044
you're enjoying the read.

00:05:04.044 --> 00:05:05.489
So thank you guys again for watching

00:05:05.489 --> 00:05:06.621
I believe in you.

00:05:06.621 --> 00:05:08.367
I hope you continue to believe in yourself

00:05:08.367 --> 00:05:10.338
and whatever your one word is.

00:05:10.338 --> 00:05:11.601
Much love and I'll see you guys

00:05:11.601 --> 00:05:14.804
again tomorrow morning for
another shot of Entspresso.

00:05:14.804 --> 00:05:17.326
♫ I wake up every morning

00:05:17.326 --> 00:05:20.909
♫ Entspresso keep me going

00:05:23.509 --> 00:05:28.153
- I always tell people the
biggest benefit to my career

00:05:28.153 --> 00:05:29.476
was probably in the beginning of things,

00:05:29.476 --> 00:05:32.546
I hated the most, like how long it took me

00:05:32.546 --> 00:05:37.293
to get to where I feel was
where I was getting my just due.

00:05:37.293 --> 00:05:39.386
My first album came of course at the crib

00:05:39.386 --> 00:05:41.897
it's going crazy just
got to make it got to go

00:05:41.897 --> 00:05:43.234
and wonder woman everything.

00:05:43.234 --> 00:05:45.690
And our nucleus on the East Coast,

00:05:45.690 --> 00:05:48.279
but I wasn't as successful
as I wanted to be

00:05:48.279 --> 00:05:51.806
for a very long time, but the older I get

00:05:51.806 --> 00:05:55.245
the more I appreciated that process

00:05:55.245 --> 00:05:56.839
that learning curve.

00:05:56.839 --> 00:05:59.608
The ability to grow gradually so

00:05:59.608 --> 00:06:03.264
I didn't have to learn
everything in front of everybody.

00:06:03.264 --> 00:06:06.973
I didn't get catapulted
immediately into success.

00:06:06.973 --> 00:06:09.564
That gave me appreciation
for the journey to get

00:06:09.564 --> 00:06:13.008
to success, it gave me
appreciation, it made me work hard.

00:06:13.008 --> 00:06:14.831
That's why I work this
hard as I do now today

00:06:14.831 --> 00:06:17.638
cause I feel like if
"Got to make it" would've

00:06:17.638 --> 00:06:20.215
billboard chart topper
success, my first single ever,

00:06:20.215 --> 00:06:22.103
I don't think I'd have
the same work ethic,

00:06:22.103 --> 00:06:22.936
just be honored.

00:06:22.936 --> 00:06:26.103
I love to do music so I'll always rap.

00:06:27.069 --> 00:06:27.928
The funny thing about
it is when I was rappin'

00:06:27.928 --> 00:06:31.454
and singing it was
something out of this world.

00:06:31.454 --> 00:06:33.105
Oh he's going to sing and rap?

00:06:33.105 --> 00:06:34.266
But he's an R&amp;B singer.

00:06:34.266 --> 00:06:35.593
And the beauty I love about music nowadays

00:06:35.593 --> 00:06:39.760
is that you have artists that
almost everybody do both.

00:06:41.215 --> 00:06:43.847
I think that's a great part
of the evolution of music

00:06:43.847 --> 00:06:47.758
is artists being creative
and believing in themselves

00:06:47.758 --> 00:06:49.903
no matter what box that
people try to put 'em in.

00:06:49.903 --> 00:06:51.630
Cause no matter what you
trying to do with your life

00:06:51.630 --> 00:06:53.574
other people going to try
to put you in this box,

00:06:53.574 --> 00:06:55.639
so you got to push through.

00:06:55.639 --> 00:06:59.551
- But I'm not in it just for the money,

00:06:59.551 --> 00:07:04.072
you know the cars, cars,
clothes, hoes, I suppose.

00:07:04.072 --> 00:07:08.297
And that's the tricky
thing about that song

00:07:08.297 --> 00:07:11.398
when I say I suppose it's kind
of like thinking in hindsight,

00:07:11.398 --> 00:07:12.968
it that really what success is?

00:07:12.968 --> 00:07:14.510
No it's not.

00:07:14.510 --> 00:07:16.537
That's what success is perceived to be

00:07:16.537 --> 00:07:18.487
and what we're taught that it is

00:07:18.487 --> 00:07:19.989
through the TV, through movies,

00:07:19.989 --> 00:07:21.953
through videos, etcetera.

00:07:21.953 --> 00:07:24.875
But success is really what
makes you happy in your heart.

00:07:24.875 --> 00:07:26.353
Making music makes me happy.

